IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ll81-nouns`
IMPORT `ll81-cross-references`

-- Row il-81. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS, and the printed values pinned: the sound readings kept beside each defect. They pass.
-- Each control shows that the test finds what it looks for where it is there, so that the failing test in ll81-tests-red.l4 is a reading of the pages and not a test that cannot succeed.
-- The expected values are written from the quotation lines in ll81-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the values there.
-- The Interpretation Law's sections 1 and 25 are pinned in the last block.

§ `Tests of the controls, item I1`

-- The two pages print the year word of the title of the 1957 law differently: SH 575 without the letter he before it, SH 1123 with it. The two strings are therefore not equal, and each holds the words of the title and the year as the other does.
#ASSERT NOT (`the title in the citing words is the title in the table's sub-heading` `the citing words of item I1` `the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)
#ASSERT (`the citing words of item I1`)'s `the name or title the citing words give` EQUALS (CONCAT "חוק בתי המשפט, ", "תשי״ז–1957")
#ASSERT (`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the title inside that sub-heading` EQUALS (CONCAT "חוק בתי המשפט, ", "ה", "תשי״ז–1957")
#ASSERT CONTAINS ((`the citing words of item I1`)'s `the name or title the citing words give`) "חוק בתי המשפט, "
#ASSERT CONTAINS ((`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the title inside that sub-heading`) "חוק בתי המשפט, "
#ASSERT CONTAINS ((`the citing words of item I1`)'s `the name or title the citing words give`) "תשי״ז–1957"
#ASSERT CONTAINS ((`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the title inside that sub-heading`) "תשי״ז–1957"

-- The number inside the mark printed beneath the margin note of section 41 is the previous-section cell of the row whose new-section cell is 41: two printed places agree.
#ASSERT `the previous-section cell printed against the new cell` "41" ((`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS JUST "19"
#ASSERT `the number inside the mark printed beneath the margin note of section 41` EQUALS "19"
#ASSERT `the previous-section cell printed against the new cell` "41" ((`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS JUST (`the number inside the mark printed beneath the margin note of section 41`)
#ASSERT (`section 41 of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the mark printed beneath the margin note` EQUALS JUST "[ב/19]"
#ASSERT (`section 41 of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `its number as printed` EQUALS "41"
#ASSERT (`section 41 of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `its margin note` EQUALS "ערעור"

-- The pairs (new, previous) as printed, read by the same test: (40, 18), (41, 19), (42, 20), and the two rows that show the middle block following the right-hand block, (34, 12) and (35, 13).
#ASSERT `the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` `the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it` "40" "18"
#ASSERT `the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` `the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it` "41" "19"
#ASSERT `the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` `the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it` "42" "20"
#ASSERT `the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` `the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it` "34" "12"
#ASSERT `the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` `the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it` "35" "13"

-- What the table prints against the number the citing words give, pinned: 41, and not 19. The lookup finds exactly one row, and finds nothing where the previous cell is absent.
#ASSERT `the new-section cell printed against the previous cell` "19" ((`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS JUST "41"
#ASSERT `the number of rows that print the previous cell` "19" ((`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the new-section cell printed against the previous cell` "99" ((`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` `the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it` "19" "19")

-- The citing words and the table, as typed.
#ASSERT (`the citing words of item I1`)'s `the number the citing words give` EQUALS "19"
#ASSERT (`the citing words of item I1`)'s `the subsection the citing words give` EQUALS JUST "(ב)"
#ASSERT (`the citing words of item I1`)'s `the place in the Law` EQUALS "section 77(ד)"
#ASSERT (`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the heading of the new-section column` EQUALS "הסעיף החדש"
#ASSERT (`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the heading of the previous-section column` EQUALS "הסעיף הקודם"
#ASSERT (`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the sub-heading of the block that opens it` EQUALS "ב. חוק בתי המשפט, התשי״ז–1957:"
#ASSERT count ((`the comparison table of SH 1123 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS 5

-- The 1969 issue is earlier than the 1984 issue, and each date is the one the footer prints.
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued before the second` `Sefer HaChukim 575` `Sefer HaChukim 1123`
#ASSERT NOT (`the first instrument was issued before the second` `Sefer HaChukim 1123` `Sefer HaChukim 575`)
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 575`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 27 7 1969)
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 1123`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 8 1984)

-- The consolidation's heading line of section 77 carries no tag (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY).
#ASSERT count `the tags the consolidation's heading line of section 77 carries` EQUALS 0

