#ASSERT `the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` `the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it` "29" "(2)18"
#ASSERT `the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` `the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it` "29" "20"
#ASSERT `the number of rows that print the new cell` "29" ((`the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the previous-section cell printed against the new cell` "31" ((`the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS JUST "19"
#ASSERT `the new-section cell printed against the previous cell` "20" ((`the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS JUST "29"
#ASSERT `the new-section cell printed against the previous cell` "99" ((`the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT count ((`the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it`)'s `the rows the row types`) EQUALS 5

-- The Ordinance's name in the citing words is the same string as the name in item (1) of the footnote on the title of NH 18, and as the heading of the table.
#ASSERT (`the citing words of item I2`)'s `the name or title the citing words give` EQUALS `the name of the ordinance in item (1) of the footnote on the title of NH 18`
#ASSERT (`the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it`)'s `the title inside that sub-heading` EQUALS `the name of the ordinance in item (1) of the footnote on the title of NH 18`
#ASSERT `the title in the citing words is the title in the table's sub-heading` `the citing words of item I2` `the comparison table of NH 18 as the row types it`
-- The words of section 129 as SH 575 prints them hold the word for "interested" with one yod, as the page prints it, and not with the two the consolidation prints.
#ASSERT CONTAINS ((`the citing words of item I2`)'s `the citing words`) "צד מעונין"
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS ((`the citing words of item I2`)'s `the citing words`) "צד מעוניין")
#ASSERT `the sentence the footnote on the title of NH 18 prints` EQUALS "נוסח חדש זה בא במקום שתי אלה"

-- The words the citing words use for what they cite are in the citing words, and are the defined words of an entry printed in section 29 (the same string in two places).
#ASSERT CONTAINS ((`the citing words of item I2`)'s `the citing words`) `the words the citing words of item I2 use for what they cite section 20 for`
#ASSERT `the words the citing words of item I2 use for what they cite section 20 for` EQUALS "תעודה ציבורית"
#ASSERT (`section 29 of NH 18 as the row types it`)'s `the defined words of an entry the row types` EQUALS JUST `the words the citing words of item I2 use for what they cite section 20 for`

-- The footnote under section 129 and item (1) of the footnote on the title of NH 18 print the same words for the volume.
#ASSERT `the volume the footnote under section 129 gives` EQUALS `the volume item (1) of the footnote on the title of NH 18 gives`

-- The issue date of NH 18 is NOTHING (no page read prints one); the Law's issue date is the one the footer prints.
#ASSERT `Dinei Medinat Yisrael, Nusach Chadash 18`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`the first instrument was issued before the second` `Sefer HaChukim 575` `Dinei Medinat Yisrael, Nusach Chadash 18`)
#ASSERT (`the citing words of item I2`)'s `the number the citing words give` EQUALS "20"
#ASSERT (`the citing words of item I2`)'s `the place in the Law` EQUALS "section 129"
