#ASSERT count `the instructions deposited here that print a status word for a section named in section 160` EQUALS 1

§ `Tests of the controls, item I4`

-- The words of section 72(a) as the 1969 page prints them contain no word of the cited title; the insertion of 1997 does. The test returns the empty result where the word is absent and a hit where it is present.
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS `the words of section 72(a) as SH 575 prints them` `the probe string for the word the cited title contains`)
#ASSERT CONTAINS ((`the instruction of SH 1634 section 5`)'s `the string it puts in`) `the probe string for the word the cited title contains`
#ASSERT `the inserting instruction names the string` `the instruction of SH 1634 section 5` `the probe string for the word the cited title contains`

-- SH 1807 section 1 prints the cited title string as the one that ends: the test finds it in the instruction's left-hand words.
#ASSERT `the short title in the citing words is the title printed before the instruction` `the citing words of item I4` `the instruction of SH 1807 section 1`
#ASSERT (`the instruction of SH 1807 section 1`)'s `the title before the instruction` EQUALS "חוק הבזק, התשמ״ב–1982"
#ASSERT (`the instruction of SH 1807 section 1`)'s `the title after the instruction` EQUALS "חוק התקשורת (בזק ושידורים), התשמ״ב–1982"
#ASSERT (`the instruction of SH 1807 section 1`)'s `the commencement the pages read print` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the instruction of SH 1807 section 1`)'s `the margin note` EQUALS "החלפת שם החוק"

-- SH 3238 prints a title of the form of the new title.
