#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 1634`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 5 8 1997)
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 1807`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 9 8 2001)
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 3238`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 4 7 2024)

-- The replay, checked step by step against the printed instructions with CONCAT of typed parts.
-- Step of 1997: the clause the page wrote is the string the instruction puts in.
#ASSERT `the clause after the step of 1997` EQUALS (`the instruction of SH 1634 section 5`)'s `the string it puts in`
-- Step of 2001: the clause before is the part before, the string replaced, the part after; the clause after is the part before, the replacement, the part after.
#ASSERT `the clause is the part before, the string, and the part after` `the part of the clause before the string replaced in 2001` ((`the instruction of SH 1807 section 97`)'s `the string it replaces`) `the part of the clause after the string replaced in 2001` `the clause after the step of 1997`
#ASSERT `the clause is the part before, the string, and the part after` `the part of the clause before the string replaced in 2001` ((`the instruction of SH 1807 section 97`)'s `the string it puts in the place`) `the part of the clause after the string replaced in 2001` `the clause after the step of 2001`
-- Step of 2024: the same, on the clause after the step of 2001.
#ASSERT `the clause is the part before, the string, and the part after` `the part of the clause before the string replaced in 2024` ((`the instruction of SH 3238 section 2`)'s `the string it replaces`) `the part of the clause after the string replaced in 2024` `the clause after the step of 2001`
#ASSERT `the clause is the part before, the string, and the part after` `the part of the clause before the string replaced in 2024` ((`the instruction of SH 3238 section 2`)'s `the string it puts in the place`) `the part of the clause after the string replaced in 2024` `the clause after the step of 2024`
-- The string replaced in 2024 occurs once in the clause at that step (counted over the words split on spaces), and the words joined with single spaces are the clause.
#ASSERT `the words joined with single spaces` `the words of the clause after the step of 2001, split on spaces` EQUALS `the clause after the step of 2001`
#ASSERT `the number of times the word occurs among the words` ((`the instruction of SH 3238 section 2`)'s `the string it replaces`) `the words of the clause after the step of 2001, split on spaces` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count `the words of the clause after the step of 2001, split on spaces` EQUALS 11
-- Each step does what its instruction says: the replaced string is gone from the clause after 2001, the new string is in it, and the clause after 2024 contains the string put in.
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS `the clause after the step of 2001` ((`the instruction of SH 1807 section 97`)'s `the string it replaces`))
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the clause after the step of 2001` ((`the instruction of SH 1807 section 97`)'s `the string it puts in the place`)
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the clause after the step of 2024` ((`the instruction of SH 3238 section 2`)'s `the string it puts in the place`)
-- The clause after each step still ends with the words the cited title is in, and the cited title is in all three.
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the clause after the step of 1997` ((`the citing words of item I4`)'s `the name or title the citing words give`)
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the clause after the step of 2001` ((`the citing words of item I4`)'s `the name or title the citing words give`)
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the clause after the step of 2024` ((`the citing words of item I4`)'s `the name or title the citing words give`)

